  + [authority_basis_sha256] is 8B2B13EDDD722EA620CE0886CB24BB4CACC35FEE111C134EEB93DAEFBFB1A0BE
  + [completed_dependency] is docs/coordination/P7_Work_Claim_Assignment_Candidate_And_Dispatch_Refusal_Contract.v1.sop
  + [completed_dependency_sha256] is 6F05A01F5B644F8BE76786B82C36DDF318A66C54A27C79A526E18F499BD67412
  + [completed_dependency_review] is docs/reviews/P7P9_DR03_Completion_Review.v1.sop
  + [completed_dependency_review_sha256] is BAB264A803D8AD58301B5753DA4D19C7EFBC9D617E045A7687319A67FF793C0D

  = must: define cross-surface carriers and rendezvous packets as projection contracts, not transport implementation
  = must: preserve typed collaboration kernel authority over IRC, Matrix, web, Codex, terminal, browser, mailbox, Langflow, narrative, debug, and manager surfaces
  = must: require authority notices, freshness notices, and dispatch refusal notices on every carrier that can be mistaken for command authority
  - never: implement IRC, Matrix, web, browser, terminal, Codex, mailbox, Langflow, MCP, adapter, transport, UI, scheduler, assignment, dispatch, operations control, or live machine control

| [CarrierKind] is (
  mailbox_file |
  IRC_message |
  Matrix_event |
  web_event |
  browser_event |
  Codex_thread_message |
  terminal_output |
  Langflow_node |
  narrative_entry |
  debug_projection |
  manager_projection |
  worker_packet_projection
)

| [CarrierDeliveryState] is (
  projected |
  queued_for_projection |
  observed |
  stale |
  refused |
  superseded |
  unknown
)

| [InboundCarrierAction] is (
  observe_only |
  source_preserving_intake_required |
  claim_review_required |
  stale_review_required |
  human_override_review_required |
  operations_dry_run_review_required |
  dispatch_refused |
  live_control_refused
)

& [CarrierNoticeRecordContract] is the record contract for a cross-surface carrier notice
  + [carrier_notice_uuid] is required stable UUID for the carrier notice record
  + [conversation_uuid] is required parent conversation identity
  + [carrier_kind] is exclusive CarrierKind
  + [surface_projection_uuid] is optional surface projection reference
  + [carrier_address] is projection-specific address or label
  + [payload_summary] is bounded description of the carrier payload
  + [payload_ref] is optional reference to external carrier location
  + [source_authority_ref_set] is set of source_document, canonical_specification, or signed_review references cited by the payload
  + [claim_ref_set] is set of coordination claim references cited by the payload
  + [assignment_candidate_ref_set] is set of assignment candidate references cited by the payload
  + [operation_request_ref_set] is set of operation request references cited by the payload
  + [authority_notice] is required
  + [freshness_notice] is required
  + [dispatch_refusal_notice] is required when assignment, dispatch, operation, approval, or live-control language is present
  + [delivery_state] is exclusive CarrierDeliveryState
  + [inbound_action] is exclusive InboundCarrierAction

  = must: keep payload_summary and payload_ref non-authoritative until source-preserving intake accepts them
  = must: preserve carrier_kind as transport provenance, not truth status
  = must: require dispatch_refusal_notice when carrier payload mentions "run", "assign", "dispatch", "approve", "control", "start", "stop", "kill", "delete", "credential", "network", "GPU", "process", "job", or equivalent operational intent
  = must: mark inbound_action source_preserving_intake_required when payload attempts to change source, canonical, or requirements
  - never: treat a carrier notice as mailbox IO authority
  - never: treat an observed carrier as proof that a participant accepted a task
  - never: treat a carrier address as credential or network permission

& [RendezvousPacketProjectionContract] is the record contract for a cross-surface rendezvous packet
  + [rendezvous_packet_uuid] is required stable UUID for the packet projection
  + [conversation_uuid] is required parent conversation identity
  + [participant_ref_set] is set of participant_uuid values involved in the rendezvous
  + [claim_ref_set] is set of related claim_uuid values
  + [purpose] is bounded rendezvous purpose
  + [coordination_question] is the open coordination question being carried
  + [proposed_next_route] is source_preserving_intake, claim_review, stale_review, human_override_review, operations_dry_run_review, completion_review, or blocked
  + [authority_basis_set] is set of source_document, canonical_specification, signed_review, or accepted state references
  + [carrier_notice_set] is set of carrier_notice_uuid references
  + [rendezvous_state] is proposed, active, stale, resolved, superseded, refused, or unknown
  + [dispatch_authority_present] is false
  + [live_control_authority_present] is false

  = must: preserve rendezvous packets as coordination projections and review prompts
  = must: include proposed_next_route when the rendezvous asks for decision or handoff
  = must: set dispatch_authority_present false and live_control_authority_present false in current scope
  - never: treat rendezvous_state active as a command, assignment, dispatch, or live-control approval

& [ConversationSurfaceProjectionContract] is the rule for projecting conversation state across surfaces
  + [conversation_uuid] is the durable kernel identity
  + [surface_projection_uuid] is the surface-specific identity
  + [surface_kind] is Codex, terminal, IRC, Matrix, web, browser, mailbox, Langflow, narrative, debug, manager_view, or worker_packet_view
  + [projected_subject_set] is source authority, canonical authority, narrative anchor, claim, assignment candidate, carrier notice, rendezvous packet, operation request, dry-run result, completion review, or fault
  + [projection_status] is current, stale, blocked, contradicted, refused, or unknown
  + [projection_notice] is required
  + [source_trace_set] is required for authority-bearing projected subjects

  = must: project conversation state from kernel records, not infer kernel records from surface scrollback
  = must: preserve projection_status separately from source truth status
  = must: require source_trace_set for any projected subject that can influence planning
  - never: collapse multiple surface threads into one conversation_uuid without explicit lineage review
  - never: let a surface projection write source authority directly

& [ReadCursorAndFreshnessProjectionContract] is the rule for durable carrier cursors and freshness notices
  + [read_cursor_uuid] is required stable UUID for cursor projection
  + [conversation_uuid] is required parent conversation identity
  + [carrier_kind] is exclusive CarrierKind
  + [carrier_address] is projection-specific address or label
  + [last_seen_carrier_ref] is optional carrier payload reference
  + [last_read_message_timestamp_ms] is optional mailbox-style cursor value
  + [cursor_state] is current, stale, blocked, ambiguous, superseded, or unknown
  + [cursor_notice] is required

  = must: treat read cursors as carrier projection state, not authority
  = must: mark cursor_state stale when carrier ordering, timestamp, or lineage is ambiguous
  = must: preserve unread carrier notices as review prompts
  - never: allow read cursor advancement to delete or overwrite carrier evidence

& [CrossSurfaceInboundActionClassification] is the rule for actions entering through a carrier or surface
  + [inbound_action_ref] is carrier_notice_uuid, surface_projection_uuid, external payload ref, or unknown
  + [classification] is exclusive InboundCarrierAction
  + [classification_basis] is source change, claim change, review request, stale signal, human override, operation request, dispatch request, live-control request, or observe-only signal
  + [safe_route] is source_preserving_intake, claim_review, stale_review, human_override_review, operations_dry_run_review, dispatch_refusal, live_control_refusal, or observe_only

  = must: classify before mutation
  = must: route source changes to source_preserving_intake
  = must: route claim changes to claim_review
  = must: route operation-looking requests to operations_dry_run_review or refusal
  = must: route dispatch-looking requests to dispatch_refusal
  = must: route live-control-looking requests to live_control_refusal
  - never: execute an inbound action directly from a carrier

& [P7CarrierAndRendezvousBoundary] is the P7 boundary opened by this contract
  + [P7P9-DR05_precondition] is accepted participant identity, claim and dispatch refusal contract, carrier notice contract, rendezvous packet projection, conversation surface projection, read cursor projection, and inbound action classification
  + [P7P9-DR05_ready_state] is ready_after_completion_review
  + [P7P9-DR05_expected_output] is docs/coordination/P7_Conflict_Staleness_Human_Override_And_Completion_Review_Contract.v1.sop
  + [P7P9-DR05_model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [P7P9-DR05_model_route_reason] is conflict and override behavior controls multi-agent safety and later operations-manager handoffs
  + [P9_dependency_note] is P9 operations-manager safety remains gated until P7P9-DR05 accepts conflict, staleness, and human override behavior

  ! [P7P9DR04VerificationSatisfied] is accepted
    @ [support] [CarrierNoticeRecordContract]
    @ [support] [RendezvousPacketProjectionContract]
    @ [support] [ConversationSurfaceProjectionContract]
    @ [support] [ReadCursorAndFreshnessProjectionContract]
    @ [support] [CrossSurfaceInboundActionClassification]
    @ [support] [P7CarrierAndRendezvousBoundary]

